From 32431573002e7fd56f34c5008ad4f905d344ea22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TeamHarrisCali <34009957+TeamHarrisCali@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 23:50:46 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Deep sleep with the lid closed (w99k)

- ARM7: FIFO_POWER_CMD_SLEEP: refuses with the lid open; LED blink, IE = lid
  open only, HALTCNT = 0xC0 (what the DSi BIOS's SWI 7 does; no BIOS calls in
  the interrupt handler); restores and answers 'awake'.
- ARM9: nds_deep_sleep() holds the SD request lock, halts (CP15 WFI) with only
  the FIFO interrupt until 'awake', then moves the clock on by the RTC delta.
  /proc/dsisettings 'deepsleep' and 'lidsleep 0|1'; /proc/dslid shows both.
- /boot/sleep: Wi-Fi down, sync, sleep, Wi-Fi Auto again after.
- dsautolog: checks /proc/dslid every second; lid closed 5 s with lidsleep=1
  runs /boot/sleep.
- Settings: 'Lid: off / sleep' button.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
